{"about":"fab3fe93125ba81777325fc75a4b1873217880cd612e89c5f659b2b669bb771b","body":"The conjecture must not conflate 'rational decision' with 'probabilistic inference'; it is required to show exactly how acting on the best-tested theory is rational in Popper's specific sense (critical preference) without implicitly relying on the very inductive principle that past success predicts future reliability, which Popper explicitly rejected.","kind":"mini.commitment-proposal.v1"}